00:24:35.000 --> 00:25:28.000
understanding the applicant. And we can talk about that further, if you like. But there's a technology for gathering the job applicants' characteristics. So those could be audio, video. The audio could be processing tone, which again might be problematic, but the language, you know, trying to extract themes out of what people say and maybe supplement the human interviewer in terms. of reminding the interviewer, the things that were said and the themes that emerged. In other words, it could be a hybrid approach rather than pure AI potentially. Other technologies are game-based assessment, so we all have probably heard ads like, hey, get online, play this game, and you can see what jobs are right for you.

