Tests are a way of letting employers know what an applicant. looks like, what are their strengths and areas in need of development? And that then gets considered with other pieces of information. And again, the tenets of fairness apply to all aspects of the application. So it's not like a test score determines your fate in these systems, as much as we might put weight on these scores as we have sometimes hear about in the news, whether it's personality, the persona series that you mentioned, or standardized testing in college admissions. No admissions office is relying solely on test scores, I don't imagine.

